WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.890
All right, let's talk about something that
I think probably some people in the audience

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:11.570
are just not going to be thrilled that that
I'm talking about, but this upcoming election

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.850
is of such utmost and total importance.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:23.140
The removal of Donald Trump is such an existential
imperative that we can't have anybody handing

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:30.500
Trump any gift, any fodder whatsoever that
he may be able to use to get himself reelected.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:36.039
And unfortunately, yesterday, Donald Trump
was handed a gift as a video went viral of

00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:42.089
a group of Black Lives Matter protesters in
Washington, D.C., surrounding and intimidating

00:00:42.089 --> 00:00:49.239
and screaming at a random woman who was just
sitting outside at a restaurant and demanding

00:00:49.239 --> 00:00:53.789
that she raise her fist and show solidarity
with protesters.

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:55.319
We have video.

00:00:55.319 --> 00:01:00.359
It's literally video of a mob surrounding
a random woman and screaming at her.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.920
This is the opposite of what we need right
now.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.230
This is exactly the type of video that the
right can use to criticize protesters.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.930
And quite frankly, this is perfect video to
help Trump.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:15.340
If you were trying to help Trump, this is
exactly what you would stage in film.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.740
I'm going to show you the video.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.990
I'll describe it.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:19.330
It's a crowd of video.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:24.320
It's a video of a crowd of people with fists
raised, a really tightly gathered around a

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.610
woman who's sitting outdoors at a restaurant
in D.C.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:30.890
They're so close to her that she's literally
leaning back with her head almost up against

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.890
the wall.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:32.890
Take a look.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:33.890
Take a listen.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:02:05.310
If you're not watching.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:09.369
Here's another video, a little more zoomed
out where you can see sort of the bigger picture

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:13.060
scene, you're also going to see a protester
asking that white people step forward.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:19.019
I guess they thought the optics of white people
intimidating the woman would somehow be better.

00:02:19.019 --> 00:02:20.019
I don't know.

00:02:20.019 --> 00:02:40.950
Take a look.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.810
So listen, guys, there's just no defending
this.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:43.810
We shouldn't even.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.319
I don't want anybody to even try to defend
it.

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:50.109
We were better off if we just say this isn't
the right strategy.

00:02:50.109 --> 00:02:51.109
This is a disaster.

00:02:51.109 --> 00:02:52.829
This is stupid activism.

00:02:52.829 --> 00:02:54.749
This is counter-productive activism.

00:02:54.749 --> 00:02:57.930
And I know that there are going to be some
people who are going to write to me and they'll

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:01.120
say, David, you privileged?

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.379
Whatever.

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:04.879
How dare you criticize this?

00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:08.420
Protesting shouldn't just be when it's comfortable.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:12.860
If this woman is sitting outside having, you
know, a 14 dollar cocktail, I don't know what

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:13.860
she's having.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.549
But what you know, whatever it is, people
are going to say, who are you to say it's

00:03:18.549 --> 00:03:21.139
not okay to make her uncomfortable?

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:23.700
Activism isn't always comfortable.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:31.049
We don't if we only protested when and where
they say it's okay, we would never get anywhere.

00:03:31.049 --> 00:03:36.510
What I'm telling you is that this is counterproductive.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:42.659
The woman who was surrounded said later she's
with the protesters.

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:45.829
She's previously marched with protesters.

00:03:45.829 --> 00:03:49.379
But here she felt under attack.

00:03:49.379 --> 00:03:55.319
These are not only intimidation tactics, they
are dumb intimidation tactics.

00:03:55.319 --> 00:04:00.140
The they are handing gifts to Trump when they
do things like this.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.180
There's no upside to this.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.400
She was already on their side.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:10.059
I don't know of anyone who was lukewarm who's
going to see this and say, oh, I like now

00:04:10.059 --> 00:04:11.900
I'm joining the movement.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.029
The movement gains nothing from this.

00:04:14.029 --> 00:04:15.730
It doesn't help the cause.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.889
Now, does it maybe make the protesters feel
good in some way?

00:04:19.889 --> 00:04:24.009
Maybe I'd feel terribly if I was there intimidating
this woman.

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:28.330
Maybe there are people who feel good when
they do something like this, but it achieves

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.330
nothing.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.729
We don't have to talk about the morality or
the ethics.

00:04:31.729 --> 00:04:37.879
We can just be pragmatists and and recognize
it plays directly into Donald Trump's hands.

00:04:37.879 --> 00:04:43.560
I actually am asking myself, do they care
if Trump gets reelected because there's a

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.560
reality?

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:51.729
I don't know the specifics of of the politics
of these individuals, but there are people.

00:04:51.729 --> 00:04:56.000
Who see Biden as just as much the enemy as
Donald Trump.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:02.479
And if that's the case, they may not care
that this type of thing plays directly into

00:05:02.479 --> 00:05:04.520
Donald Trump's hands.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.349
If that's the case, that's a big problem.

00:05:06.349 --> 00:05:07.740
It's a different problem.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.990
And I would disagree with them.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.720
And, you know, we could figure that out.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.030
I've discussed that problem ad nauseum for
months.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:17.639
But why are we giving people ammunition?

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:18.759
What are what are we doing?

00:05:18.759 --> 00:05:20.740
This is completely counterproductive.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.440
And fortunately, you know, I wasn't sure.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.050
I haven't seen everybody's reaction to this.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:29.009
You know, people that that work in MySpace.

00:05:29.009 --> 00:05:34.090
But for the most part, most of the people
who I follow on Twitter on the left who have

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:36.820
tweeted about this have denounced it.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:38.099
And that's what it just needs to be.

00:05:38.099 --> 00:05:40.030
This is not what we're advocating for.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.030
This is bad.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.700
This doesn't help the movement.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:57.889
This helps Donald Trump.

00:05:57.889 --> 00:06:24.419
This

00:06:24.419 --> 00:06:34.800
is 
a bad idea.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:58.860
Hopefully, that will 
be

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:44.760
the consensus.

